Notebook[{
Cell["PadicRationalN", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"8d736011-2797-4fd5-99f6-73204855ca2a"],

Cell["\<\
PadicRationalN[m,p,e,n] represents m p^e + O(p^(e+n)); n is relative \
precision and e+n is absolute precision. A zero significand with e=Infinity \
denotes exact zero; finite e denotes an uncertain zero. Normal attempts \
bounded rational reconstruction and otherwise returns m p^e; an uncertain \
zero gives Missing[\"InsufficientPrecision\",e+n]. Sqrt requires even \
valuation and a square unit, selects a deterministic local branch, and \
returns n relative digits for odd p or n-1 for p=2. Uncertain zero or \
insufficient binary digits gives Missing[\"InsufficientPrecision\"]; a proved \
nonsquare gives Indeterminate with Padic::sqrt. Prefer PadicN for finite \
snapshots; direct construction does not validate fields.\
\>", "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"3c2ca2e1-96e0-49ae-811d-db31e76cdda4"],

Cell["\<\
Prefer PadicN[r,p,n] to construct finite snapshots. Direct application of \
this representation head does not validate its fields.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ceb02df9-7794-482d-bff8-b7281697f8d6"],

Cell["\<\
Relative precision is n and absolute precision is e+n. Exact zero uses \
e=Infinity; a finite-precision zero retains an absolute-precision bound.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3c32c892-c91d-42a5-9086-09ea7223340b"],

Cell["\<\
Normal attempts reconstruction of the normalized unit and restores p^e. It \
returns the scaled integer residue when no bounded candidate passes \
validation. This alone does not certify an unknown original rational.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"483e9731-ea33-43f3-94a1-b9f5e29ce334"],

Cell["\<\
Approximate arithmetic uses residues and propagates precision, without \
rational reconstruction. Existing approximations cannot be promoted to more \
known digits or certified in another base.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ae8718f5-cfed-47d9-9e72-0e8a1ad62214"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<PadicNumbers`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "ExampleInitialization",ExpressionUUID->"901a3d14-ea18-4d3a-9608-\
d7f41693f9d4"],

